//? Title: Ridders root finding: actual corrected brackets and distinct stopping reasons
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Find a zero of a continuous scalar function starting from a sign-changing
interval. Ridders combines a midpoint evaluation with an exponential
interpolation correction inside a sign-changing bracket. The actual native
callback stream replaces report-local solver replays. The original
square-root-of-two problem and native bisection comparison remain.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Given ordered endpoints a,b with opposite callback signs, let c=(a+b)/2. The
correction is
$$ d=c+(c-a)\frac{\operatorname{sign}(f(a)-f(b))f(c)}{\sqrt{f(c)^2-f(a)f(b)}}. $$
\alttext(Ridders uses the actual midpoint value and opposite-sign endpoint values to correct the query within its bracket.)
The native implementation normalizes callback magnitudes in widened arithmetic
before forming the radicand, then safeguards a rounded correction outside the
open bracket by reusing the midpoint. Exact midpoint zeros require no second
callback. Local quadratic convergence needs the usual regularity assumptions. A
sign-changing discontinuity is not a continuous root; interval resolution and
residual success remain separate recorded stop reasons.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ridders_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto f = [](double x) { return x * x - 2; };
    auto t = a::ridders_trace(f, 1, 2);
    const auto &s = t.steps[0];
    std::print("| actual initial a | b | midpoint | f(midpoint) | actual candidate | f(candidate) | second " "query |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | " "{} |\n",
               s.a, s.b, s.midpoint, s.midpoint_value, s.candidate,
               s.candidate_value, s.correction_evaluated);
    g::Diagram d(48, 1100);
    d.node("n0", {0, 0}, std::format("Actual midpoint {:.8g}", s.midpoint));
    d.node("n1", {5, 0}, std::format("Actual correction {:.8g}", s.candidate));
    d.node("n2", {10, 0}, std::format("Actual final root {:.8g}", t.result.root));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/ridders_tiny.svg");
}
```
